  "name": "Seeing, Maintaining, and Learning: The Evolution of Multimodal Agent Memory",
  "notes": "A broad literature synthesis spanning images, video, audio, GUI and embodied settings. Its GUI section compares interface-state retention, action outcomes, cross-session reuse and visual evidence, but the paper does not provide a new GUI-agent experiment. Taxonomy corpus counts and benchmark classifications are authors' annotations, not independently audited field coverage. Updating stored content alone does not establish the survey's self-evolving-policy tier; endpoint task success does not isolate memory use. Lifecycle, resource-budget and provenance recommendations are proposed evaluation directions rather than demonstrated guarantees. Platform facets stay unspecified; cited systems and releases were not independently verified.",
  "published_at": "2026-10-14",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "adjacent",
  "summary": "Surveys multimodal memory using representation and management axes, distinguishing fixed-policy updates from policy evolution and comparing GUI memory evaluation with other modalities.",
